From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: take the userpd id from the AHB data

With the multiPD series (openwrt/openwrt#25393) the userpd id of a radio
is a member of struct ath11k_ahb, not of struct ath11k_base, so the line
ath11k_nss_init() logs when a SoC registers with the firmware no longer
builds on IPQ5018. Read it through ath11k_ahb_priv() on the AHB bus and
print 0 for a PCI radio, which has no user PD.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  */
 #include <linux/of.h>
 
+#include "ahb.h"
 #include "debug.h"
 #include "mac.h"
 #include "nss.h"
@@ -3084,7 +3085,8 @@ static int ath11k_nss_init(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 
 	ab->nss.if_num = ath11k_nss_get_interface_type(ab);
 
-	ath11k_info(ab, "nss init soc nss if_num %d userpd_id %d\n", ab->nss.if_num, ab->userpd_id);
+	ath11k_info(ab, "nss init soc nss if_num %d userpd_id %d\n", ab->nss.if_num,
+		    ab->hif.bus == ATH11K_BUS_AHB ? ath11k_ahb_priv(ab)->userpd_id : 0);
 
 	if (ab->nss.if_num >= NSS_MAX_NET_INTERFACES) {
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "NSS invalid interface\n");
